WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — jouleos (180s) Narrator Bobby

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.141
First, today's computers stack many separate layers, and AI agents are bolted on top unchanged.

2
00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:14.158
Second, none of those layers asks beforehand how much energy an agent's action will actually spend.

3
00:00:14.718 --> 00:00:21.614
Third, an agent machine must measure energy, enforce strict budgets, and refuse actions that break them.

4
00:00:22.174 --> 00:00:29.683
New agent-safety platforms add sandboxes, external watchdogs, and policy wrappers on top of Linux, macOS, or Windows

5
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:37.580
kernels. That engineering solves real file and network containment problems, yet it treats the underlying process model as

6
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:45.477
permanently fixed—where an agent remains an ordinary guest program and no kernel gates commits on certified energy bounds.

7
00:00:46.037 --> 00:00:52.918
Before naming any commercial product, our study teaches the ten-step stack from bare silicon, chip, board, and

8
00:00:52.918 --> 00:01:00.863
firmware through instruction sets, hardware abstraction, kernels, compilers, and programs right up to the human interface. Even

9
00:01:00.863 --> 00:01:08.620
formally verified microkernels prove functional C code correctness while saying nothing at all about joules or power limits.

10
00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:17.960
Closing that architectural gap requires four linked open contracts: an energy-oriented schedule ordered cheapest operator first rather

11
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:27.002
than billed in tokens, narrowing capability-and-joule grants checked outside the AI model, transactional commits bounded by preconditions,

12
00:01:27.002 --> 00:01:35.651
postconditions, invariants, and joule ceilings, and an eight-step isolation ladder carrying honest hardware or estimator meter tags.

13
00:01:36.211 --> 00:01:42.687
Even built-in processor energy counters on modern chips are partly mathematical models rather than inline wire

14
00:01:42.687 --> 00:01:50.457
shunts, missing operand-level variations. Our monotone lattice algebra tests all seventy-eight thousand four hundred pairs of sensor

15
00:01:50.457 --> 00:01:57.168
boundaries and attribution rules so combining a hardware shunt with an estimate always preserves the weaker label.

16
00:01:57.728 --> 00:02:04.971
In our three-dimensional stack view, authorization runs strictly outside the language model, and every tool response

17
00:02:04.971 --> 00:02:12.839
arrives tagged as untrusted passive data rather than executable instructions so poisoned prompts cannot hijack control. Before

18
00:02:12.839 --> 00:02:20.769
any actuation begins, the runtime reserves a crash-safe energy hold and settles a hash-chained cryptographic receipt afterward.

19
00:02:21.329 --> 00:02:28.782
Across seven Rust workspace crates, three hundred ten automated conformance tests verify deterministic binary encoding

20
00:02:28.782 --> 00:02:36.803
without floating-point ambiguity, reject revoked, duplicate, or over-budget calls, replay exact ledger balances after simulated

21
00:02:36.803 --> 00:02:43.308
power loss, and automatically drop net energy splits whenever host idle power drifts past five percent.

22
00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:50.256
This white paper is written as an honest architectural review and requirement guide, never an inflated

23
00:02:50.256 --> 00:02:58.837
product pitch. Ratios cited from the private Joule Operating System repository—such as hundred-thousand-fold corpus efficiency claims—are

24
00:02:58.837 --> 00:03:06.791
explicitly flagged as unverified project claims rather than measurements, and bare-metal external power metering remains unset.
